      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t have any context into the storage issue here, so I cannot speak to that. But regarding the user code:\n\nWhen does this storage code get exercised? Does this mean that cleanupPreCreatedUsers() can now be called even not during boot-up? Is that safe? I believe this method is currently only called at boot, and perhaps relies on that assumption.\nIn particular, what if someone is trying to upgrade a pre-created user into a full user at the same time? Might we wind up *slating* the pre-create for removal, then upgrading it, and only then removing it (thereby destroying a regular user!)?\n\nAny thoughts Felipe?",
